.SH NAME
pause \- stop until signal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pause( )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Pause
never returns normally.
It is used to give up control while waiting for
a signal from
.BR kill (2)
or
.BR alarm (2).
The signal received must not cause termination or be 
currently set up
to be ignored by the calling process.
If the signal is
.I caught
by the calling process (see
.BR signal (2))
and control is passed back from the signal catching
function,
the calling process resumes execution from the point of suspension;
pause returns a value of -1
and
.B errno 
is set to EINTR.
.SH SEE ALSO
kill(1), kill(2), alarm(2), signal(2), setret(3).
.SH ASSEMBLER
.nf
.na
	CONSTANT PAUSE	:= 29

	sc	#PAUSE
.fi
.ad
